        "abstract": "Titration is a quantitative method for determining an unknown property (typically concentration) of an analyte. In a recirculating water system, the reagent is returned to the system, and in many circumstances it is desirable to ensure that the quantity of reagent is minimized. We describe an automated instrument for executing titrations in flowing streams that is well suited to recirculating water systems.",
